  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="e6cd-873b-fa56-9146" name="Han Dynasty: Three Kingdoms (Art of War) - List Notes" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false">
      <description>THREE KINGDOMS (The Art of War, pp.116-119). Special rules: Heroic Combat (see the Heroic Combat section), Military Strategist (a single Ruse per 1,000 points, 50 pts each, paid from the Special Units allowance and not counted in victory points unless used; not built), Army Musician (units within 18" may re-roll rally attempts, Flee dice and Panic tests; used once), Sworn Brotherhood, the Brotherhood of the Peach Garden. Steadfast (Liu Bei): may re-roll one Leadership test during a game; never subject to a further re-roll. Guile, Courage, Master Strategist and Impetuous as given on the characters. Percentage limits are by points. "May only have one selected option per 1,000 points" for Special Units is documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Three Kingdoms]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  THREE KINGDOMS ARMY. Characters up to 25% (0-1 Warlord, Yang or Yin). Cavalry up to 33%. Infantry at least 33%. Special Units up to 25% (only one selected option per 1,000 points). Army variants (allies are documented only): the Army of Wei may take Wuhuan (Eastern Steppe Nomads) and Yellow Scarves; the Army of Shu-Han may take Xi Yi (Early Eastern Tribes); the Army of Wu may take Man Yi (Early Eastern Tribes).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
